            <div id="cite-apa" class="tab selected" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-0" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_apa rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_apa rendering_contributiontojournal_apa"><a rel="Person" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/persons/judith.aldridge/" class="link"><span>Aldridge, J.</span></a> (2019). <a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/publications/does-online-anonymity-boost-illegal-market-trading/" class="link"><span>Does Online Anonymity Boost Illegal Market Trading?</span></a> <span><em>Media, Culture and Society</em></span>. <a onclick="window.open(this.href, '_blank','noopener,noreferrer'); return false;" href="https://doi.org/10.1177/0163443719842075" class="link"><span>https://doi.org/10.1177/0163443719842075</span></a></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-author" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-1" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_author rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_author rendering_contributiontojournal_author"><a rel="Person" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/persons/judith.aldridge/" class="link"><span>Aldridge, Judith</span></a>. / <a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/publications/does-online-anonymity-boost-illegal-market-trading/" class="link"><span><strong>Does Online Anonymity Boost Illegal Market Trading?</strong></span></a>. In: <a rel="Journal" href="#" class="link"><span>Media, Culture and Society</span></a>. 2019.</div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-BIBTEX" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-2" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_bibtex rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_bibtex rendering_contributiontojournal_bibtex"><div>@article{46719311988c4a4f9d45b46b7efa5ff2,</div><div>  title     = "Does Online Anonymity Boost Illegal Market Trading?",</div><div>  abstract  = "Anonymity allows the online trade in illegal products and services on cryptomarkets to flourish in spite of being enacted in a public location. Bolstered by the extensive media coverage of the cryptomarket trade in drugs, fraud and weapons, these platforms may function as a kind of criminal {\textquoteleft}gateway{\textquoteright}, and in so doing facilitate {\textendash} or indeed amplify {\textendash} criminality. I argue, however, that researchers must establish {\textendash} not assume {\textendash} that the criminality facilitated by online anonymity will exclusively and uniformly produce more harmful outcomes. I consider here two possibilities in connection to the cryptomarket trade in illegal drugs: reduced drug market violence and reduced drug harms to users. Whether these potential {\textquoteleft}benefits{\textquoteright} are viewed as valuable will vary and depend substantially on the perspective and interests of the observer, including drug sellers, drug buyers, law enforcement officials, and academic researchers.",</div><div>  keywords  = "Online anonymity, cryptomarkets, Darknet, illegal drugs, harm reduction, drug markets, violence",</div><div>  author    = "Judith Aldridge",</div><div>  year      = "2019",</div><div>  doi       = "10.1177/0163443719842075",</div><div>  language  = "English",</div><div>  journal   = "Media, Culture and Society",</div><div>  issn      = "0163-4437",</div><div>  publisher = "Sage Publications Ltd",</div><p>}</p></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-harvard" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-3" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_harvard rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_harvard rendering_contributiontojournal_harvard"><a rel="Person" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/persons/judith.aldridge/" class="link"><span>Aldridge, J</span></a> 2019, '<a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/publications/does-online-anonymity-boost-illegal-market-trading/" class="link harvard_title"><span>Does Online Anonymity Boost Illegal Market Trading?</span></a>', <span><em>Media, Culture and Society</em></span>. <a onclick="window.open(this.href, '_blank','noopener,noreferrer'); return false;" href="https://doi.org/10.1177/0163443719842075" class="link"><span>https://doi.org/10.1177/0163443719842075</span></a></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-standard" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-4" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_standard rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_standard rendering_contributiontojournal_standard"><a rel="ContributionToJournal" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/publications/does-online-anonymity-boost-illegal-market-trading/" class="link"><span><strong>Does Online Anonymity Boost Illegal Market Trading?</strong></span></a> / <a rel="Person" href="https://research.manchester.ac.uk/en/persons/judith.aldridge/" class="link"><span>Aldridge, Judith</span></a>. <br />In: <span>Media, Culture and Society</span>, 2019.<p class="type"><span class="type_family">Research output<span class="type_family_sep">: </span></span><span class="type_classification_parent">Contribution to journal<span class="type_parent_sep"> › </span></span><span class="type_classification">Article</span><span class="type_classification"><span class="type_parent_sep"> › </span>peer-review</span></p></div>
            </div>
        
            <div id="cite-RIS" class="tab " role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-5" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="rendering rendering_researchoutput  rendering_researchoutput_ris rendering_contributiontojournal rendering_ris rendering_contributiontojournal_ris"><p>TY  - JOUR</p><p>T1  - Does Online Anonymity Boost Illegal Market Trading?</p><p>AU  - Aldridge, Judith</p><p>PY  - 2019</p><p>Y1  - 2019</p><p>N2  - Anonymity allows the online trade in illegal products and services on cryptomarkets to flourish in spite of being enacted in a public location. Bolstered by the extensive media coverage of the cryptomarket trade in drugs, fraud and weapons, these platforms may function as a kind of criminal ‘gateway’, and in so doing facilitate – or indeed amplify – criminality. I argue, however, that researchers must establish – not assume – that the criminality facilitated by online anonymity will exclusively and uniformly produce more harmful outcomes. I consider here two possibilities in connection to the cryptomarket trade in illegal drugs: reduced drug market violence and reduced drug harms to users. Whether these potential ‘benefits’ are viewed as valuable will vary and depend substantially on the perspective and interests of the observer, including drug sellers, drug buyers, law enforcement officials, and academic researchers.</p><p>AB  - Anonymity allows the online trade in illegal products and services on cryptomarkets to flourish in spite of being enacted in a public location. Bolstered by the extensive media coverage of the cryptomarket trade in drugs, fraud and weapons, these platforms may function as a kind of criminal ‘gateway’, and in so doing facilitate – or indeed amplify – criminality. I argue, however, that researchers must establish – not assume – that the criminality facilitated by online anonymity will exclusively and uniformly produce more harmful outcomes. I consider here two possibilities in connection to the cryptomarket trade in illegal drugs: reduced drug market violence and reduced drug harms to users. Whether these potential ‘benefits’ are viewed as valuable will vary and depend substantially on the perspective and interests of the observer, including drug sellers, drug buyers, law enforcement officials, and academic researchers.</p><p>KW  - Online anonymity</p><p>KW  - cryptomarkets</p><p>KW  - Darknet</p><p>KW  - illegal drugs</p><p>KW  - harm reduction</p><p>KW  - drug markets</p><p>KW  - violence</p><p>UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85064538826</p><p>U2  - 10.1177/0163443719842075</p><p>DO  - 10.1177/0163443719842075</p><p>M3  - Article</p><p>SN  - 0163-4437</p><p>JO  - Media, Culture and Society</p><p>JF  - Media, Culture and Society</p><p>ER  - </p></div>
